	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element " >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<h4><strong><span style="font-size: 16px;">Energy Equivalents</span></strong></h4>
<p>1 watt = is a very small amount of power, roughly the energy it takes to lift a 1 pound weight 1 foot</p>
<p>1 kilowatt hour (kWh) = 1,000 watts or a 100 watt light bulb on for 10 hours</p>
<p>1 Megawatt hour (MWh) = is equal to 1 million watts or 1,000 kWh</p>
<p>The Average US household uses = 11,280 kWh (2011 average annual electric consumption)</p>
<p>The average US coal power plant produces = 231,000,000,000 kWh (231 billion)</p>
<p>The average US nuclear power plant produces = 790,000,000,000 kWh (790 billion)</p>

